<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Kladsko</h1><p class="st-meta">1459 CE – 1742 CE · capital Kłodzko</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A mountain-ringed county on the Bohemian-Silesian border, created by George of Poděbrady in 1459 and won by Prussia in 1742.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klodzko">Kłodzko</a> (Glatz) Land, a basin enclosed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudetes">Sudeten</a> mountains, had long belonged to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a>, though at times it was held by Silesian dukes. In 1459 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-of-podebrady">George of Poděbrady</a>, king of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, raised it to a county and granted it to his sons, who also held the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-ziebice">Duchy of Ziębice</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The county passed through several hands before coming under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in the 16th century. Its fortress at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klodzko">Kłodzko</a> guarded the road from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Silesia</a> into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> spread widely until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation</a> restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> after 1622. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glassmaking">Glassmaking</a>, linen weaving and spa towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kudowa-zdroj">Kudowa</a> and Duszniki supported the economy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1742 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick II of Prussia</a> annexed the county with most of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Silesia</a>, and it was incorporated into Prussian Silesia. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, and its German population was expelled.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-kladsko.jpg" alt="County of Kladsko" width="320" height="312"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:County_of_Kladsko_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1459 CE – 1742 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kłodzko</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>George of Poděbrady, Henry the Elder of Münsterberg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Czech</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>County of Glatz, Grafschaft Glatz</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1600&amp;focus=county-of-kladsko" aria-label="County of Kladsko on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5060 428 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Kladsko lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5380 684L5330 692M5380 684L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5330 692h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5380 684h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5380 684h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1600&amp;focus=county-of-kladsko">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

